  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0003 database is a comprehensive system for managing user accounts, teams, and billing information. At its core, it contains a users table, which stores information about each registered user, including their name, email address, password, and two-factor authentication details. Each user can be associated with a team, which is stored in the teams table, and teams are owned by a single user, as indicated by the owner_id foreign key in the teams table. The announcements table tracks important messages sent to users, while the api_tokens table stores authentication tokens for users. The invitations table manages invitations sent to users to join teams, and the invoices table keeps track of billing information for both users and teams. The notifications table stores notifications sent to users, and the password_resets table stores tokens for password reset requests. The performance_indicators table contains metrics about the system's performance, including recurring revenue and new user growth. Subscriptions for both users and teams are stored in the subscriptions and team_subscriptions tables, respectively, and the team_users table links users to the teams they belong to.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context:\n\nThis project involves the development of a software as a service (SaaS) application framework using Laravel, a popular PHP framework. The framework, known as Laravel Spark, is designed to simplify the creation of SaaS applications by providing prebuilt modules for common functionalities such as billing, team management, and user subscriptions.\n\nObjectives:\n\nThe primary objective is to provide developers with a streamlined toolset that reduces the time and effort required to build and deploy SaaS applications. This includes offering integrated subscription plan management and a user-friendly billing portal for customers to manage their subscriptions.\n\nStakeholders & Users:\n\n- Developers: Utilize Laravel Spark to streamline the creation of SaaS applications.\n- End Users: Individuals or teams who subscribe to the SaaS service provided by applications built on Spark.\n- Administrators: Manage subscription plans, user data, and billing processes.\n\nFunctional Descriptions:\n\n1. Subscription Management:\n   - Define various subscription plans.\n   - Allow users to subscribe to different plans.\n   - Enable users to update their subscription plans.\n\n2. Billing Management:\n   - Provide customers with a billing portal.\n   - Allow users to manage payment information and download invoices.\n\n3. Team Management:\n   - Facilitate team creation and handle team-specific subscriptions.\n   - Manage team roles and user invitations to join teams.\n\n4. Notification System:\n   - Send notifications to users.\n   - Implement functionality for announcements and updates.\n\n5. API Token Management:\n   - Create and manage API tokens for user access.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions:\n\n- Scalability: The system must support multiple concurrent users and efficient database operations.\n- Security: Ensure secure handling of user data, especially billing information.\n- Usability: The user interface should be intuitive and accessible for both administrators and end users.\n- Maintainability: The system should be easy to update and maintain by developers.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0003.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0003\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `two_factor_auth` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams` (\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teams_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcements` (\n  `announcement_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `message` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`announcement_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api_tokens` (\n  `token_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`token_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `api_tokens_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invitations` (\n  `invitation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invitation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invitations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `invitations_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invoices` (\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invoice_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoices_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `invoices_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notifications` (\n  `notification_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`notification_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notifications_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `password_resets` (\n  `reset_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reset_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `password_resets_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `performance_indicators` (\n  `indicator_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `recurring_revenue` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `new_user_growth` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `report_date` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`indicator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscriptions` (\n  `subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`subscription_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `team_subscriptions` (\n  `team_subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_subscription_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `team_subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `team_users` (\n  `team_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `team_users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `team_users_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
